!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the lifecycle of a proveo-rendered sbx Kit and its deterministic sandbox
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox_stale_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/run.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/launch_receipt.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/launch_receipt_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/stop_signal_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/clone_carry_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/teardown_end_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/report.go (reportReattach, keptSandbox, listedSandbox, keptPorts)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/report_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/list.go (Listed.Ports)
' covers: internal/choiceui/blocked_run.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/blocked_run.go
'
' ── A KEPT SANDBOX MUST NOT SILENTLY OVERRIDE THIS RUN (2026-09-27) ─────────
' Re-attach passes the name only, so a kept sandbox runs with the Kit, image
' and env it was CREATED with. Measured: a hermes run with the host-chrome add-on
' ticked re-attached to a sandbox kept from an earlier run; PID 1 and the agent
' still carried the earlier PROVEO_EGRESS_SESSION_ID, PROVEO_HOST_CDP_PORT never
' arrived, and the agent drove the in-sandbox headless Chromium. sbx's help says
' -e "takes effect on a re-attach too"; proveo never passes it there.
' The fix is a RECEIPT written at creation (os.UserCacheDir()/proveo/
' sbx-sandboxes/<name>.json): image + local image ID, Kit digest, clone, mounts,
' and a digest per env var, with the session ID normalised to <sid> (two dry
' runs then compare identical). On reuse:
'   same receipt            → re-attach, as before
'   changed, headed         → ask. Yes runs the three steps for every harness:
'     carry clone and agent state home, sbx rm --force, create the same name.
'     retireIfStale prints "replacing <name> — <changes> changed"; retireSandbox
'     prints each step's line only as that step starts, so a hung carry never
'     shows the create line (2026-10-22; TestRetireReportsEachStepOnlyWhenItStarts).
'     The lines stay on screen, so they carry no "n/3" (R1 review, 2026-11-11):
'     "carrying its work home from <name>", "sbx rm --force <name> — deleting
'     it and its session", "<name> — this run creates it anew".
'     The session does not persist. Host proveo files stay.
'     No keeps it. [y/N] and [esc] are each a left-aligned row. The last row
'     records the typing and the line under it says enter submits. Enter on
'     y or yes is the yes above. Enter on anything else, or esc, is the no.
'     A running one is re-attached and the new settings do not apply.
'     A stopped one stays. This run stops, and the next proveo run asks again:
'     the error reads "sandbox <name> kept; the next proveo run reattaches and
'     asks again", and the `sbx rm --force` sentence is a run-log row (R2: the
'     operator answered, so no how-to on screen; decision E).
'     A re-attach's "`sbx rm --force <name>` builds it fresh next run" is a
'     run-log row too (R2).
'   changed, not headed, stopped → the same three steps, no question
'   changed, not headed, running → warn. The session stays. The new settings do not apply.
' WHAT EACH BRANCH PRINTS (output-readability R1, 2026-11-11). A kept running
' sandbox: "⚠ <name> — kept running without this run's changes", dim "not
' applied: <changes>", then "the next proveo run reattaches to it" (headed no)
' or "`sbx rm --force <name>` deletes it and its session; the next run builds
' it fresh" (not headed). retireIfStale returns those changes (kept), and the
' re-attach facts flag "⚠ workspace — <name> keeps the mode and mounts it was
' created with" (whichever of clone and mounts they name), or "⚠ workspace —
' <name>'s mode and mounts are unrecorded" for a sandbox with no receipt. The
' reason, "the workspace block is this run's plan, not <name>'s", goes to the
' run log alone (Item.Log, P6, R1 round 3): that block printed this run's ✓
' outcome before the stale step (R1 review; pinned by
' TestAReattachToAnUnrecordedSandboxFlagsTheWorkspaceBlock and
' TestAReattachWithNoRecordClaimsNothingAndFlagsAKeptWorkspaceMode).
' Run reads `sbx ls` ONCE for the stale step:
' sbx.Exists before it, staleChanges(name, now, exists) off that answer, and
' reuseOrCreate(cfg, exists) after it, exists cleared by a retire.
' THE RE-ATTACH PRINTS THE SANDBOX'S OWN RECORD, never this run's settings,
' which the branches above may not have applied: image, kit dir, cpus and
' memory from the receipt (it records the kit dir, cpus, memory and the -p
' list for this alone; changes ignores them, so none marks a sandbox stale),
' mounts from sbx's own row (`sbx ls --json`; a ":ro" workspace prints
' "(ro)"). A kit dir `proveo clean` removed reads dim "no longer on disk".
' The secrets this run stored for it lead the same Facts block (P3).
' CPUS AND MEMORY UNDER SBX'S DEFAULTS STAY UNPRINTED. MEASURED 2026-11-11,
' sbx v0.50.0, read-only: `sbx ls --json` and `--format yaml` carry name, id,
' agent, status, last_used_at, ports, workspaces, workspace_missing and
' created_at, no CPU and no memory; no other verb reads a sandbox back
' (`sbx --help`; docs.docker.com release notes name `sbx ls` JSON fields up
' to 0.51.0, none of them resources). sbx's create block prints them once
' ("CPU: 14", "Memory: 24 GiB" on a run that set neither), and `sbx create
' --help` states the defaults (cpus 0 = all host CPUs; memory 50% of host,
' 512 MiB–32 GiB). So the receipt holds cpus/memory only when proveo passed
' --cpus/--memory (PROVEO_SBX_CPUS, PROVEO_SBX_MEMORY, PROVEO_SBX_INSTANCES),
' and the re-attach prints them only then; proveo does not re-derive sbx's
' defaults. A receipt written before KitDir and Publish existed prints
' neither (left as is).
' PORTS: a running row's own ports; a STOPPED row lists none, so keptPorts
' reads the receipt's -p list instead. MEASURED 2026-11-11 on sbx v0.50.0 with
' a sandbox created for the check and removed after: `sbx create -p
' 127.0.0.1:47123:8080` → running row lists 47123→8080; `sbx stop` → the row
' has no "ports" key and `sbx ports` says "No published ports"; `sbx run -d`
' → the row lists 47123→8080 again. A receipt written before this field reads
' nil (unknown), one with no ports an empty list. A missing record prints
' nothing for it and the run log says so. The receipt stays a record here, not a source of clone
' mode (clone-workspace.puml). The start line is "● re-attach to <name> —
' left by an earlier run" with "`sbx rm --force <name>` builds it fresh next
' run" dim under it; the reason a re-attach is safe (the name derives from
' this workspace, so its workspace is this one) goes to the run log. An
' OpenCode engine ensureOpenCodeEngine just created reads "● attach to <name>".
' OPENCODE ENGINES (D2, DONE (wt) 2026-10-17, MEASURED;
' _spec/defs/opencode/engine-local-history.puml): the opencode-only refusal is
' gone, so an OpenCode engine follows the same rule. After PreserveClone and
' before SaveState and the rm, retire carries its database home (the user's
' D1, "Carry the DB over"), and the headed prompt adds "Its OpenCode history
' moves to the new sandbox." An export failure keeps the engine; a legacy
' keeper engine (D7) carries nothing, the new engine imports from the V2
' share, and retire deletes its legacy owner record after the rm.
' HISTORY (keeper design): a headed yes removed a running sandbox except an
' OpenCode engine with active, unpublished, or unattested state, which had to
' be recovered before replacement.
' A screen that fails to open counts as no, so a stopped sandbox is not removed.
'
' ── A FORWARDED STOP TEARS DOWN LIKE A NORMAL EXIT AND EXITS 128+sig ────────
' DECIDED 2026-10-17, twice. Teardown: the user chose "Stop runs normal
' teardown". Exit status: the user chose "Exit 128+sig, 'stopped'
' (Recommended)". MEASURED (internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go Run):
'   forwardStop returns (ctx, stop, cancel, signalled func() syscall.Signal);
'     signalled is 0 when proveo cancelled the run itself (Ctrl+C remove).
'   stopOutcome(runErr, sig, forced) returns (teardown, result). For sig != 0
'     and not forced: teardown nil, result backend.Stopped{sig}. Otherwise both
'     are runErr. The signal is read ONCE, after the retry block.
'   Run prints "● <target> — stopped by SIGTERM" (or SIGHUP) first under
'     results; "teardown runs as on a normal exit" is a run-log row (R2).
'     Teardown takes the SUCCESS branch: clone edits and commits lifted, state
'     saved, `sbx rm`; an OpenCode engine is retained.
'   Run returns Stopped, and cmd/proveo main's exitCode maps it to 128+signal:
'     143 for SIGTERM, 129 for SIGHUP (_spec/internal/backend/exit-code.puml).
'     The transcript reads "outcome: stopped by SIGTERM".
'   No template-reload retry after a stop: Run checks signalled() == 0 before
'     sbx.ReloadTemplate and again before the retry run. ReloadTemplate takes
'     no context, so a stop during the reload waits for it to finish. Since
'     review #5 the retry also requires !forceRemove.Load(), so a Ctrl+C remove
'     never relaunches (MEASURED, sandbox.go:1560).
'   After the first signal, later SIGTERM/SIGHUP are swallowed until teardown
'     ends — by design: the scheduler SIGTERMs, then kill-session (SIGHUP)
'     after termGrace = 1 min (internal/schedule/runner.go:37), and a longer
'     teardown must not be cut short. Only SIGKILL interrupts a hung teardown.
' [Inference] A signal that lands after the agent failed — while its sbx
' client is still exiting, or after run() returns but before stopOutcome reads
' signalled() — turns that real failure into Stopped: normal teardown, exit
' 143, and the sandbox holding the failure evidence is removed. The sbx
' client's own exit after the agent ends, plus the retry block, bound that
' window.
' HISTORY: before 2026-10-17 a stop read as a failed run ("kept for
' diagnosis", no `sbx rm`). An earlier revision that day made a stop exit 0;
' the exit-status decision replaced it. Pinned by
' TestAForwardedStopTearsDownLikeANormalExitAndReportsTheSignal (the
' stopOutcome table, including the Ctrl+C remove path, sig 0 + forced, and "a
' signal after the operator chose remove") in teardown_end_test.go, which has
' no build tag so Windows CI runs it; and by TestACancelWithoutASignalIsNotAStop
' and TestHangupCancelsTheRunInsteadOfKillingProveo in stop_signal_test.go
' (!windows: they send real signals). The run context is `runCtx` (MEASURED).
'
' ── WHAT A NORMAL END DOES WITH THE SANDBOX: normalEndOf (2026-10-17) ──────
' MEASURED, sandbox.go: after TeardownClone, SaveState and the home-access
' commit, Run's success branch switches on normalEndOf(forced, stranded,
' retainsEngine), a pure function:
'   forced (the operator chose Ctrl+C remove) → endRemove, always
'   stranded != nil (work still only in the sandbox) → endKeepStranded, even
'     for an OpenCode engine, which closes on "⚠ <name> — kept: <err>, with
'     its OpenCode history" and the `proveo rm` fix (R2)
'   retainsEngine (opencodeTarget) → endRetainEngine, which closes on "✓
'     retained engine <name> — holds OpenCode's history"; `sbx rm --force
'     <name>` deletes it, a run-log row since R2 (engine-local-history.puml)
'   otherwise → endRemove
' Pinned by TestANormalEndRemovesTheSandboxUnlessWorkOrTheEngineStaysInIt
' (teardown_end_test.go, untagged).
'
' ── RESIDUALS, RECORDED NOT FIXED (2026-10-17 review #4) ────────────────────
'   * A HUNG TEARDOWN. SaveState and `sbx rm` carry no timeout, and
'     proveo swallows signals after the first. A hung proveo can outlive the
'     scheduler's kill-session, and its late `rm` can remove a same-named
'     sandbox a later run has reattached to. A per-name lock or a teardown
'     deadline would close it. Pre-existing; a stop widens the exposure
'     (reported; the missing timeouts MEASURED by reading the calls).
'     PARTLY CLOSED 2026-10-22 (user: "Drop P1, probe + deadline", "36s probe
'     3m others"). MEASURED incident: sbx 0.49.2 could not boot any VM on the
'     host (POST /sandbox/<name>/start 502 after 875s; every shim stalled after
'     "creating container task"), so the retire's clone-mode probe `sbx exec`
'     on the stopped sandbox waited forever while all three step lines were
'     already on screen. boundCommand (sandbox.go) now bounds every guest
'     call on the carry path: the probe at cloneProbeDeadline = 36s; snapshot,
'     rebase, span, remote fetch, bundle, lift and the .env read at
'     guestExecDeadline = 3m. A timeout reads as the error it replaces, so
'     an unanswered probe leaves the mode unknown and the sandbox kept
'     (STRANDED), never removed. The receipt stays out of it (review #6).
'     STILL OPEN: SaveState and teardown's `sbx rm`. sbx's own rm on a clone
'     sandbox starts the container first, and hung the same way; the decided
'     next step is a 3m deadline plus a rescue recipe, never an automatic shim
'     kill (killing the shim made the daemon respawn it and stall again).
'     DONE for the retire path (2026-10-24): removeRetired runs `sbx rm` through
'     guestRun (3m); a timeout keeps this run stopped and names `sbx ls` and the
'     rm to repeat once sbx answers.
'     Pinned by TestAGuestThatNeverAnswersKeepsTheSandboxInsteadOfHangingTheRun.
'     CLOSED 2026-11-10 (tui-upgrades-delivery.puml, T1): SaveState and
'     teardown's `sbx rm` run through guestRun (3m), as do the reflog read and
'     the pushed-branch fetch. A removal that times out prints the warning and
'     `sbx ls`, then `sbx rm --force <name>`. _spec/internal/backend/teardown.puml.
'     Pinned by TestTeardownDeadlineEndsEveryGuestCallThatNeverAnswers.
'   * HISTORY: a stop during the retry's prepareOpenCodeLaunch was honoured
'     only after it returned (its prepare and recover steps allowed up to
'     15 min each). D2 (DONE (wt)) replaced it with ensureOpenCodeEngine's
'     create + one-time import, which takes no context (MEASURED) — so a stop
'     during the retry's import waits for it, as during ReloadTemplate.
'   * The forced Ctrl+C remove returns the raw runErr. Reported: it can print
'     "context canceled" and exit 1, or "agent exited with code -1" and exit
'     255 when WaitDelay SIGKILLs the sbx client. Pre-existing.
'   * CLOSED by D2 (DONE (wt)): removeOpenCodeEngine, a third `sbx rm` path that
'     skipped PreserveClone, went with opencode_cache.go (MEASURED absent). The
'     D5 path in ensureOpenCodeEngine `sbx rm`s only a FRESH engine after a
'     failed import, before any agent ran in it.
'   * The forced Ctrl+C remove after a failed carry prints the rescue recipe,
'     then deletes; the modal warns about uncommitted changes, not about
'     commits that were never carried (review #5, reported).
' The kept-for-diagnosis hint names `sbx exec -it <name> bash` (MEASURED),
' matching https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/sbx/exec/.
'
' ── WORK STRANDED IN THE SANDBOX KEEPS THE SANDBOX (2026-10-17) ─────────────
' MEASURED: PreserveClone and TeardownClone return an error while work remains
' only in the sandbox — snapshot failed ("uncommitted work is still only in
' <name>"), carry failed ("the agent's branches are still only in <name>"), or
' the clone mode is unknown ("cannot tell whether <name> holds a clone…").
' (R2, 2026-11-11: the stranded errors now say "it", the kept line names the
' sandbox, and the fix reads `proveo rm [--stop] <name>` in both teardown and
' retire; _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml.)
' Normal-exit and stop teardown then skip `sbx rm`, print "<err> — <name> kept;
' `sbx rm --force <name>` deletes it once the work is home", keep home access
' and print the IDE attach. retireSandbox (the stale-sandbox upgrade,
' launch_receipt.go) returns the same error before SaveState and `rm`. The
' forced Ctrl+C remove still deletes: its dialog says "Uncommitted changes can
' be permanently lost" (internal/choiceui/sandbox_close.go). Detail:
' _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml.
' AN UNANSWERED SANDBOX MAY BE REMOVED ON A HEADED YES (2026-10-24, user:
' "Offer remove-anyway"). MEASURED incident: sbx 0.49.2 could not boot the
' v2-era proveo-claudecode-f8781ef6 (57-layer image), so every retire stopped
' at "cannot tell whether … holds a clone" and blocked the v3 run until the
' operator removed it by hand. Its branches already sat under
' refs/sandboxes/<name>/ (sbx's own mirror; proveo never writes there).
'   sandboxClone wraps errNoCloneAnswer only when the probe hit
'     cloneProbeDeadline. An unreadable answer or a later hang (snapshot,
'     bundle) is a guest that runs, so it keeps the old STRANDED rule.
'   retireSandbox on errNoCloneAnswer: mirroredRefs lists
'     refs/sandboxes/<name>/*; confirmUnansweredRemoval shows them
'     (choiceui.UnansweredRemovalCopy, ≤ 6 then "… and N more").
'     yes → removeRetired: no SaveState, no OpenCode history carry (both exec
'       in the guest); the prompt says that history is lost.
'     no, non-headed, or no screen → error "<probe err> — <name> kept; its
'       branches are mirrored under refs/sandboxes/<name>/ (N refs)" (or
'       "nothing of it is mirrored on the host"), and the run stops.
'   Pinned by TestAnUnansweredSandboxIsRemovedOnlyOnAYesThatNamesItsMirroredRefs
'   (clone_carry_test.go) and TestTheUnansweredRemovalPromptListsTheMirroredRefs
'   (choiceui).
' THE SANDBOX, NOT THIS RUN, SAYS WHETHER IT CLONES (MEASURED, reviews #5-#6):
' sandboxClone(in, name) answers from in.Clone only when in.CloneKnown — this
' run created the sandbox (launchCfg.KitDir != "", set before sbx.RunArgs and
' again for the retry) — else from a strict, stdout-only guest probe of
' /run/sandbox/source, else unknown (kept). The launch RECEIPT is not a source
' (review #6 HIGH: it can be stale or missing); it only drives the change
' detection above. Run's teardown defer resolves the mode FIRST, so
' reportPushedBranches, ideFacts and TeardownClone see the real one;
' retireSandbox clears CloneKnown so the old sandbox is always asked, and
' carries into refs/proveo/<sid>-retired/* so this run's own teardown fetch
' cannot overwrite it. Detail, the failures it closes and the residuals:
' clone-workspace.puml.
title sbx Kit lifecycle — create with a Kit, reuse by name, keep failures and stranded work, remove success and stops

state "resolve full RunConfig\n+ render Kit spec.yaml" as RESOLVE
state "sandbox name exists?" as EXISTS <<choice>>
state "fresh launch config\nname + Kit + image + env + agent\n+ mounts/clone/ports/limits" as CREATE
state "receipt matches?" as DRIFT <<choice>>
state "carry clone + state home\nsbx rm --force" as RETIRE
state "reattach launch config\nname + trailing agent args ONLY" as REUSE
state "sbx run" as RUN
state "sandbox exists after error?" as CREATED <<choice>>
state "reload image template\nretry once with FULL create config" as RETRY
state "agent/session running" as LIVE
state "child result" as RESULT <<choice>>
state "preserve clone + sync state\nusing the retained FULL config" as PRESERVE
state "kept for diagnosis" as KEPT
state "kept: work still only\nin the sandbox" as STRANDED
state "sbx rm --force" as REMOVE
state "removed" as REMOVED
state "removal warning\nsandbox remains stale" as STALE
state "stopped sandbox kept\nnext run asks again" as ASKAGAIN
state "launch failed\nno sandbox to retain" as FAILED

[*] --> RESOLVE
RESOLVE --> EXISTS : WriteKit is per run;\nsecret values are never in it
EXISTS --> CREATE : no
EXISTS --> DRIFT : yes
DRIFT --> REUSE : receipt matches,\nor running and headed no,\nor running and not headed
DRIFT --> RETIRE : changed and headed yes,\nor stopped and not headed
DRIFT --> ASKAGAIN : stopped and headed no
RETIRE --> CREATE : clone carried home (refs/proveo/<sid>-retired),\nor the old sandbox was direct (guest probe)
RETIRE --> STRANDED : clone not carried, or clone mode unknown\n(retireSandbox errors; this run stops)
CREATE --> RUN
REUSE --> RUN
RUN --> LIVE : agent session opens
RUN --> CREATED : command error before session
CREATED --> RETRY : no, and no stop signalled
RETRY --> RUN : template reload succeeded\nand still no stop
RETRY --> FAILED : reload or retry failed
RETRY --> PRESERVE : a stop signalled during the reload\n(no retry run; exits 128+sig)
CREATED --> PRESERVE : yes, or a stop signalled
LIVE --> RESULT : sbx child exits
RESULT --> PRESERVE : exit != 0
RESULT --> PRESERVE : exit == 0
RESULT --> PRESERVE : SIGTERM/SIGHUP forwarded\n(teardown nil, result Stopped)
PRESERVE --> KEPT : run failed
PRESERVE --> STRANDED : snapshot or carry failed, or clone mode unknown\n(normalEndOf → endKeepStranded)
PRESERVE --> REMOVE : run succeeded, or stopped by a signal;\nproveo exits 0, or 128+sig for a stop
STRANDED --> REMOVE : operator, once the work is home
STRANDED --> [*]
REMOVE --> REMOVED : success or already absent
REMOVE --> STALE : other error; warn
KEPT --> REUSE : next proveo run,\nsame target + workspace
KEPT --> REMOVE : operator cleanup
STALE --> REUSE : next proveo run
ASKAGAIN --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]
REMOVED --> [*]

note right of CREATE
  **Creation-only fields travel once.**
  sbx accepts the Kit, template, environment,
  agent, workspace, clone, ports and limits only
  while creating the named sandbox.
end note

note right of REUSE
  **The stored spec owns a reused sandbox.**
  Passing ""--kit"" here is rejected before the
  agent starts: ""--kit can only be used when
  creating a new sandbox"".

  The same applies to every other creation-only
  field. The supported shape is:
  ""sbx run --name <existing> [-- AGENT_ARGS…]"".
end note

note bottom of PRESERVE
  **Launch config and lifecycle metadata differ.**
  Reattach strips fields from the argv, not from
  proveo's retained full config. Clone recovery
  still needs the workspace path; state sync still
  needs the host state-home environment.
end note

note bottom of KEPT
  **Failure retains evidence deliberately.**
  The next run reuses the VM by its fixed name;
  the hint names ""sbx exec -it <name> bash"" and
  ""sbx rm --force <name>"". A forwarded stop is
  not a failure since 2026-10-17.
end note

note bottom of STRANDED
  **Work only in the sandbox keeps it.** A
  failed snapshot or carry skips ""sbx rm"" and
  says so; the forced Ctrl+C remove still
  deletes, as its dialog warns.
end note

note bottom of REMOVE
  **Success is disposable.** After clone output and
  state are copied home, proveo removes the sandbox.
  A removal failure is warning-only but leaves a
  stale name that follows the reuse branch next run.
end note
@enduml
